{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0162dXh3W5NzNQmiP8p4TdAo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Lifecycle.\n2\t\n3\tInternal declarations exported by the audit_emit compatibility facade.\n4\t\"\"\"\n5\t\n6\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n7\t\n8\t__all__ = ('emit_pair_rail_review_expected', 'emit_directory_added_recorded', 'emit_notification_lifecycle', 'emit_night_mode_toggled')\n9\t\n10\t# QDSAA-FUNCAO-LONGA: Preserve the existing event schema and its field coercion together during relocation.\n11\tdef emit_pair_rail_review_expected(\n12\t    *,\n13\t    session_id: str,\n14\t    tool_name: str = \"unknown\",\n15\t    file_path_hash_prefix: str = \"\",\n16\t    review_id: str = \"\",\n17\t    timeout_ms: int = 0,\n18\t    project: str = \"\",\n19\t) -> None:\n20\t    \"\"\"Emit pair_rail_review_expected (PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 denominator).\n21\t\n22\t    Fired by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` at the point a canonical-edit\n23\t    Codex review is definitely ENTERED — only after the kill-switch,\n24\t    non-write-tool, not-L3+ and sentinel-bypass arms have all returned. It is\n25\t    the durable session-correlated DENOMINATOR for the /ceo-boot `pair_rail`\n26\t    activity-conditioned liveness row: a window session with\n27\t    expected-but-no-outcome is the S254 dead-rail class and must escalate,\n28\t    and a healthy outcome from session B must never mask session A\n29\t    (`session_id` is therefore an explicit required kwarg — the hook threads\n30\t    the Stop/PreToolUse event's own session id, not a default).\n31\t\n32\t    r5 F2 + r6 F2: `review_id` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex or exactly \"\";\n33\t    the RAW value is validated BEFORE any bounding — off-shape incl.\n34\t    oversize is DROPPED to \"\", never truncated, so two distinct off-shape\n35\t    ids sharing a 16-hex prefix can never alias to one pairing key) is\n36\t    the PER-INVOCATION correlation key — minted by\n37\t    `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` at review entry (`os.urandom(8).hex()`)\n38\t    and identical on this emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_case`.\n39\t    It is what makes the /ceo-boot pairing invocation-EXACT: counting\n40\t    (even the r4 (session, file-hash) BUCKET counting) fundamentally\n41\t    cannot pair a specific expected with its OWN case — an old completed\n42\t    case for the SAME (session, file) offset a later dead expected 1:1.\n43\t    An expected `review_id` with no matching `pair_rail_case` in-window is\n44\t    an outstanding (dead) review -> RED.\n45\t\n46\t    r4 F2 (retained as legacy fallback + harmless secondary key):\n47\t    `file_path_hash_prefix` (the SAME 16-hex SHA-256 path-prefix\n48\t    token `pair_rail_case` carries, computed by the hook with the same\n49\t    helper; bounded shape `[0-9a-f]{0,16}`, off-shape COERCED to \"\") keys\n50\t    the /ceo-boot expected/terminal pairing per (session, file-hash)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ff2ef3b-1be9-4d6b-9faf-7d08cfab8359","uuid":"35c68603-38dc-4a7b-8238-feab5f90c0e0","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:17:18.069Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/lifecycle.py","content":"\"\"\"Lifecycle.\n\nInternal declarations exported by the audit_emit compatibility facade.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n__all__ = ('emit_pair_rail_review_expected', 'emit_directory_added_recorded', 'emit_notification_lifecycle', 'emit_night_mode_toggled')\n\n# QDSAA-FUNCAO-LONGA: Preserve the existing event schema and its field coercion together during relocation.\ndef emit_pair_rail_review_expected(\n    *,\n    session_id: str,\n    tool_name: str = \"unknown\",\n    file_path_hash_prefix: str = \"\",\n    review_id: str = \"\",\n    timeout_ms: int = 0,\n    project: str = \"\",\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit pair_rail_review_expected (PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 denominator)